'''Waji rice''' ({{Langx|bl|Arroz waji}}; {{Langx|ca|Arròs d'Waji}}; {{Literal translation|[[Waajuri people|Waajuri]] rice}}) is a savory rice dish that developed in the community of [[Estuaria]] (specifically [[Navassa]]) fusing together [[W:African cuisine|West Kaftian]], [[Mesogean cuisine|Mesogean]] ([[W:Andalusian cuisine|Andalusian]], [[Volisanian cuisine|Volisanian]] and [[Burawi cuisine|Burawi]]) influences, consisting mainly of meat and/or seafood, and vegetables mixed with rice and spices.  

[[Southwestern Kaftia|Southwest Kaftians]] and [[W:Paella|Volisanian people]] each had versions of rice dishes in their respective cultures. These styles blended in Estuaria, and the resulting dish is now considered a cross between [[W:Jollof rice|Kaftian rice]] and Volisanian paella.

